{
"dur": 49.338,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 5.915,
"text": "Jensen Huang was born in Taiwan in 1963. His family later moved to Thailand.",
"end": 6.19
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.19,
"vo_start": 6.465,
"vo_end": 12.425,
"text": "When he was nine, his parents sent him and his older brother to America, to stay with an uncle and get a good education.",
"end": 12.7
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 12.7,
"vo_start": 12.975,
"vo_end": 17.925,
"text": "The uncle enrolled them at a school in rural Kentucky that he thought was a prestigious boarding school.",
"end": 18.2
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 18.2,
"vo_start": 18.475,
"vo_end": 22.715,
"text": "It was the Oneida Baptist Institute, a strict school that also took in troubled teenagers.",
"end": 22.99
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 22.99,
"vo_start": 23.265,
"vo_end": 28.064,
"text": "Jensen was the youngest boy in the dorm. His daily job was cleaning the bathrooms.",
"end": 28.339
},
{
"i": 6,
"start": 28.339,
"vo_start": 28.614,
"vo_end": 32.573,
"text": "He has said he didn't complain, and that it taught him to just get on with the work in front of him.",
"end": 32.848
},
{
"i": 7,
"start": 32.848,
"vo_start": 33.123,
"vo_end": 39.523,
"text": "His parents eventually joined them in Oregon. As a teenager he worked at Denny's, washing dishes and waiting tables.",
"end": 39.798
},
{
"i": 8,
"start": 39.798,
"vo_start": 40.073,
"vo_end": 48.388,
"text": "He studied electrical engineering at Oregon State, then designed chips at AMD and LSI Logic, and took a master's degree at Stanford at night.",
"end": 49.338
}
],
